GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC14, KNOWN_RISKS #135): the light buffers' layer mask tells a sprite
straight on the 3D scene (3) from other 2D over it (2).

GoldLink's lighting lights the 3D scene and the player's 3D sprite but left every 2D layer as the
game drew it: Fly's landing trainer, a 2D sprite, landed at full brightness and darkened as the
player's sprite took over (the user's play test, 2026-11-19). The lighting lights layer 3 as the
player. A sprite over a background (the HM cut-in's banner, a menu's cursor) stays 2.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

diff --git a/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp b/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp
diff --git a/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp b/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp
index b0c8768..2d2510e 100644
--- a/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp
+++ b/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp
@@ -1006,7 +1006,13 @@ void SoftRenderer::DrawScanline_BGOBJ(u32 line)
                 int col = i + SideShift + MaxSide;
                 if (col >= 0 && col < 256 + 2 * MaxSide)
                 {
-                    mask[col] = ((val1 >> 24) & 0xC0) == 0x40 ? 1 : ((val2 >> 24) & 0xC0) == 0x40 ? 2 : 0;
+                    // 3 (GoldLink, KNOWN_RISKS #135): a sprite straight on the 3D scene (Fly's
+                    // landing trainer, an emote bubble): lit as the player, as its 3D sprite is.
+                    // A sprite on a background (the HM cut-in's banner, a menu's cursor) isn't.
+                    // A sprite's flags: 0x10, or 0x80 semi-transparent (0xC0 | alpha a bitmap
+                    // one); a background's 0x01 << its number; the 3D layer's 0x40.
+                    mask[col] = ((val1 >> 24) & 0xC0) == 0x40 ? 1
+                        : ((val2 >> 24) & 0xC0) == 0x40 ? (((val1 >> 24) & 0x90) ? 3 : 2) : 0;
                     const u32 flag1 = val1 >> 24;
                     Fixed2D[line][col] = (flag1 & 0x40) == 0 && flag1 != 0x20 && !BlendsWith3D(i, val1, val2);
                 }
